{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "6550f3fa-7b75-8708-a8fb-f66a2ad9416e",
  "created_at": "2026-02-03T10:40:44-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Gloria Valdez",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tony Ferreira",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:36:13-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities Division, this is Tony. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:36:18-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, um, good morning. Sorry to bother you. I think I'm calling the right place? It's about a water and sewer bill."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:36:27-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You got the right place. What's going on with the bill?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:36:32-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So I got my bill and it says estimated next to the reading. Like, an estimated read. And I'm pretty sure nobody ever came to read my meter. Nobody's been in my building, I'd have known. So I don't get why I'm being charged for a guess."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:36:50-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, yeah, that happens. When an actual reading doesn't come in, whether the meter's hard to get to or the reader device didn't pick it up, the system fills in a number based on your past usage. Then it gets corrected when a real reading comes through."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:37:08-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, but that's the thing, it's higher than it should be. I'm one person in a one-bedroom. It's kind of ridiculous. Sorry, I'm not mad at you, I just, it's annoying."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:37:20-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, no, totally fair. Don't apologize. Let me ask, are you the one on the account, or does your landlord have it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:37:29-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's in my name. I rent, but the bill comes to me. Is that okay? Am I allowed to call about it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:37:38-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yep, if it's your name you're fine. What's the name on the account?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:37:44-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Gloria Valdez. V-A-L-D-E-Z."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:37:46-05:00",
      "duration": 22,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, Gloria. Give me a second to pull it up. [pause] Okay, I see it. Yeah, the last bill was flagged as an estimate. I'll put in a request for an actual meter read so it gets trued up. Once that comes in, if you were overcharged, it shows as an adjustment on the next bill."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:38:08-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So I should do that, the request? Or you do it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:38:13-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'm doing it right now. You don't have to do anything except maybe let whoever comes in, if they need to get into the building. Is a good number for you the one you're calling from?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:38:27-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's 401-555-0156. Is that right, did you get that?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:38:31-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-five-six. Perfect."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:38:33-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Um, another thing. The bill's due and I can't really pay all of it at once right now. Is a payment plan possible? Is that a thing?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:38:44-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It can be, yeah. I'd put a note on the account about the disputed estimate, and then the billing office can talk to you about splitting it up. I'll have them call you. Want me to do that?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:38:59-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, please. Thank you. And, sorry, one more. If I can't get there during the day, can I drop a payment in the box tonight? Does that count as on time, or does it have to be in before you close?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:39:15-05:00",
      "duration": 22,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There's a drop box outside City Hall, and it's emptied the next business day. Generally what matters is that it's in the box by the due date, but I'd put the due date on the check and write your account number so it matches up. You can also pay online anytime, any hour, through the city website."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:39:37-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, online, okay. So the box tonight is fine, and online is also fine? I want to make sure I'm doing it right."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:39:46-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Both are fine. Just don't pay the full amount if you're going the payment plan route until billing calls you. Hold off a day or two."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:39:56-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, I'll wait. That makes sense. Oh, and this is totally random, sorry, but I need a gift for a white elephant thing at work this week. Twenty dollars or so. Any ideas? You sound like someone who'd know."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:40:11-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Funny, I always say go with something useful that looks fancy. A good candle, or a nice set of kitchen towels. People fight over those every time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:40:22-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A candle. Okay, that's actually good. Thanks. Sorry, that wasn't a city question."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:40:28-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem at all. So, meter read request is in, billing will call about the plan. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:40:35-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, I think that's everything. Thank you so much, Tony."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:40:40-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome, Gloria. Have a good one."
    }
  ],
